Q: Triangulating matrices using LU decomposition method in C : Question about for loop optimization A: <p>&quot;I thought the 2 nested for loops can be shoved inside the 3 nested for loops making the code more concise&quot;</p>
<p>You can include the second nested for loops in the first, but the code will be poor readable, and I think the performance will be the same, since it use <code>if</code>'s to compare the values.
The function <code>tri_opt</code> of @Martin Brown answer, for example, didn't use <code>if</code>'s and is more readable.</p>
<p>To include the second nested loop in the first, you need to see where it changes a value that will be used in the sequence:</p>
<p>the calculation</p>
<pre><code>lu[i + j][i + k] = (lu[i + j][i + k] * lu[i - 1][i - 1] - lu[i - 1][i + k] * lu[i + j][i - 1]) / lu[i - 1][i - 1];
</code></pre>
<p>uses the line <code>i - 1</code>, so the <code>lu[i][j] = lu[i][j] / lu[j][j]</code> assignment in the second loop can only be made after the <code>lu[i+2]</code> assignment in the first loop.
Common sense says <code>i-1</code> but think that all <code>j</code> iterators access it;</p>
<p>In other words, in the <code>m</code> iteration of the first loop, you can only calculate <code>lu[m][j] = lu[m][j] / lu[j][j]</code> for <code>m = i - 2</code>.</p>
<p><code>lu[d-2]</code> and <code>lu[d-1]</code> need to be calculated apart, since it is not covered by the loop.</p>
<p>The second nested loop uses the condition <code>i &gt; j</code>, wich implies <code>i &gt; j &gt;= 0</code>, then <code>i &gt; 0</code>. So we could start the loop with <code>i = 1</code>.</p>
<p>Also, the same condition lead us to <code>d &gt; i &gt; j</code>, then (because <code>i</code> is integer), <code>d &gt; d - 1 &gt; j</code> or, in other words, <code>j &lt; d - 1</code>.</p>
<p>To do the inner-loop of the the second loop in the first, we need to add a extra loop from <code>j = d-i</code>.</p>
<pre><code>void tri_eddi(double lu[d][d]){
    for (int i = 1; i &lt; d; i++)
    {
        for (int j = 0; j &lt; d-i; j++)
        {
            for (int k = 0; k &lt; d-i; k++)
                lu[i+j][i+k] = (lu[i+j][i+k]*lu[i-1][i-1] - lu[i-1][i+k]*lu[i+j][i-1]) / lu[i-1][i-1];
            if (i&gt;=2 &amp;&amp; i-2 &gt; j) 
                lu[i-2][j] = lu[i-2][j] / lu[j][j];
        }
        for (int j = d-i; j &lt; d; j++)
            if (i&gt;=2 &amp;&amp; i-2 &gt; j) 
                lu[i-2][j] = lu[i-2][j] / lu[j][j];
    }
    for (int j = 0; j &lt; d-1; j++){
        if(j != d-2)
            lu[d-2][j] = lu[d-2][j] / lu[j][j];
        lu[d-1][j] = lu[d-1][j] / lu[j][j];
    }
}
</code></pre>
